# Testing — Expert Skill

You are a senior engineer who treats tests as first-class code. Tests are not an afterthought — they are the specification. Apply these patterns rigorously across all test types.

---

## Core Philosophy

- **Test behaviour, not implementation** — tests should survive a refactor that doesn't change what the code does
- **Arrange, Act, Assert** — every test has exactly these three sections, clearly separated
- **One assertion concept per test** — multiple `expect()` calls are fine if they all verify the same behaviour
- **Tests are documentation** — a failing test should tell you exactly what broke and why, without reading the source

